Z||000000||Gold-86SE||07-11-2001||07:46 PM||||<BR>Ok, how do i describe the problem.  It, for lack of a better description, feels like it is missing, which creates a bump as I drive.<P>I'll be driving down the road under an even throttle, no acceleration or decelaration, it feels like the engine kicks me in the rear and my back.  Not an excessive bump, but fairly constant.<P>This problem is on an 86 SE V6 4-spd.<P>I am not receiving any codes, yet I thought it might be the TPS, based on a recent problem with my 84 - because the symtoms appeared to be similiar.  Replaced it with another from an 85 GT and that one was bad, so I am back to my original TPS.<P>I really don't want to spend money on a part that is not the cause.  How do I trouble shoot this?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||07-11-2001||10:51 PM||||<BR>As a foot note, I disconnected the tach filter to see if there might be any difference in the engine performance.  As you might have guessed, there was none.<P>What do you think is going on?<BR>||||reg||1
