Z||000004||Gold-86SE||07-12-2001||02:08 PM||||<BR>Fiero_24, you stated, that you are experiencing the same problem, and mentioned that you were going to be "replacing the Distributor cap and rotor, fuel filter, spark plugs and wires, and if all else fails I will change the timing."<P>If I had not replaced all of these items last year, I would be right in line with you.  I think these, at an intial point, point to a maintenance related problem.  But, I replaced them already.  So, I am banking that they are not the cause, but I have the cheap AutoZone plug wires, so who knows.<P>Mach10, you said that is "Sounds like the engine is missing, then surging a little. Ignition check!"  I checked the timing and appeared to be fine.<P>Idea. How do I know if the coil is weak?<BR>||||reg||1
